1
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:03,960
Alice?

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,040
Alice, it's you, isn't it?

3
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:24,830
Yuujio!

4
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:27,160
Choose your actions carefully.

5
00:00:28,320 --> 00:00:32,440
I have the right to remove up to
70 % of your life if I wish it.

6
00:00:32,580 --> 00:00:36,756
And if you touch me again without my
permission, I will have your hand.

7
00:00:41,180 --> 00:00:42,010
Alice.

8
00:00:43,020 --> 00:00:44,080
Are you sure?

9
00:00:44,300 --> 00:00:46,888
Because it's been a
while since you saw her.

10
00:00:47,280 --> 00:00:48,980
Then we do what she says.

11
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:50,130
For now.

12
00:00:50,213 --> 00:00:54,728
Now, we can argue our case with her after
we get inside the Central Cathedral.

13
00:00:55,700 --> 00:00:56,757
Enough delays.

14
00:00:56,840 --> 00:01:00,600
Now, Elite Disciple Eugeo,
Elite Disciple Kirito,

15
00:01:00,980 --> 00:01:03,560
you are in violation of the Taboo Index.

16
00:01:04,020 --> 00:01:08,860
I will take you into custody, then
question you, then execute you.

17
00:01:25,420 --> 00:01:26,277
Theises of the Lord.

18
00:01:26,360 --> 00:01:27,190
Theского-moved.

19
00:01:27,273 --> 00:01:28,103
Rising.

20
00:01:28,186 --> 00:01:29,016
Silled.

21
00:01:29,099 --> 00:01:29,929
And the.

22
00:01:30,012 --> 00:01:30,842
Of the. In the. The.

23
00:01:30,925 --> 00:01:31,755
Beginning.

24
00:01:31,838 --> 00:01:32,668
Should. Will. Will.

25
00:01:34,800 --> 00:01:36,340
Be. Is.

26
00:01:38,120 --> 00:01:38,950
In. The.

27
00:01:39,033 --> 00:01:39,863
Take a look at the time.

28
00:01:39,946 --> 00:01:40,776
I'm ready to go.

29
00:01:40,859 --> 00:02:02,860
I'm ready to run.

30
00:02:42,760 --> 00:02:45,360
Oh, my God.

31
00:03:04,020 --> 00:03:05,300
Tiese! Ronie!

32
00:03:14,660 --> 00:03:17,180
Lady Knight, forgive our intrusion.

33
00:03:17,480 --> 00:03:21,127
We'd like to return these to our
mentors with your permission.

34
00:03:21,540 --> 00:03:22,370
Very well.

35
00:03:22,660 --> 00:03:26,060
However, I cannot allow these
criminals to carry weapons.

36
00:03:26,460 --> 00:03:27,860
I will look after them.

37
00:03:32,860 --> 00:03:34,180
You have one minute.

38
00:03:34,440 --> 00:03:36,180
Speak with them, if you wish.

39
00:03:41,320 --> 00:03:42,960
I'm sorry, Eugeo.

40
00:03:43,200 --> 00:03:46,220
You shouldn't even be
in this mess. I should.

41
00:03:46,460 --> 00:03:47,660
This is my fault.

42
00:03:47,920 --> 00:03:48,900
I was dumb.

43
00:03:49,300 --> 00:03:51,040
I acted so recklessly.

44
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:53,700
Stop it.

45
00:03:53,860 --> 00:03:54,937
You're not to blame.

46
00:03:55,020 --> 00:03:56,432
You did the right thing.

47
00:03:56,680 --> 00:03:59,757
Your friend was in trouble and
you did what you could to help.

48
00:03:59,840 --> 00:04:02,260
What happened is my fault, not yours.

49
00:04:03,180 --> 00:04:07,500
You have nothing to be sorry
about. Ever. I promise.

50
00:04:07,840 --> 00:04:10,537
Whatever it takes, I'll
become an Integrity Knight.

51
00:04:10,620 --> 00:04:13,500
And then I'll be the one
to come and save you.

52
00:04:13,680 --> 00:04:15,327
And I won't stop until I do.

53
00:04:16,280 --> 00:04:18,045
Till then, don't give up hope.

54
00:04:18,840 --> 00:04:20,680
I swear, I'll save you.

55
00:04:25,080 --> 00:04:27,560
Um, I brought you some lunch.

56
00:04:31,640 --> 00:04:34,240
Make sure to eat it before it spoils.

57
00:04:35,360 --> 00:04:36,340
Thanks, Riley.

58
00:04:37,500 --> 00:04:39,600
It is time. Step away.

59
00:04:46,380 --> 00:04:47,210
No.

60
00:05:02,020 --> 00:05:04,940
I don't know.

61
00:05:41,340 --> 00:05:43,797
I wish they'd let me
dive in there with you.

62
00:05:43,880 --> 00:05:45,409
Maybe I could get you out.

63
00:06:04,320 --> 00:06:06,180
Oh, excuse me.

64
00:06:14,160 --> 00:06:16,560
A robot!

65
00:06:34,260 --> 00:06:35,090
Hey!

66
00:06:35,620 --> 00:06:37,440
You're scaring her, Ichiemon!

67
00:06:40,880 --> 00:06:43,780
What did you call this
thing just now? His name.

68
00:06:44,180 --> 00:06:45,080
What else?

69
00:06:45,380 --> 00:06:46,520
He's Ichiemon.

70
00:06:46,740 --> 00:06:50,180
An electroactive muscled
operative machine, or EMOM.

71
00:06:50,700 --> 00:06:52,582
He's also the first of his type.

72
00:06:52,820 --> 00:06:55,173
So, like, we added the Ichie at the top.

73
00:06:56,380 --> 00:06:57,380
Ichiemon, get it?

74
00:06:58,980 --> 00:07:02,080
And what is this Ichiemon doing on board?

75
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:03,210
Well, he sort of...

76
00:07:03,293 --> 00:07:07,217
I'm using it to fine-tune a program and
Higa here is giving me a hand with it.

77
00:07:07,300 --> 00:07:10,065
We're lab partners again,
just like in college.

78
00:07:10,660 --> 00:07:11,580
Good morning.

79
00:07:13,300 --> 00:07:14,900
Morning. You sleep well?

80
00:07:18,360 --> 00:07:21,420
Your problem is its balancer's
processor runs slow.

81
00:07:21,780 --> 00:07:23,297
Can't you buy a faster chip?

82
00:07:23,380 --> 00:07:25,097
It's not like you don't
have the budget to.

83
00:07:25,180 --> 00:07:28,557
Yeah, but cooling and battery
drain would still be a problem.

84
00:07:28,640 --> 00:07:31,377
Considering that, this is
the best that we can do.

85
00:07:31,460 --> 00:07:35,497
One other option would be to tune the
EAP actuator to pick up the slack.

86
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:39,109
Sure, but the polymer muscles
are last-gen, so there's that.

87
00:07:39,300 --> 00:07:40,500
Upgrade to CNTs.

88
00:07:40,820 --> 00:07:43,820
They'll take the strain
better and make it lighter.

89
00:07:46,460 --> 00:07:48,257
We're in our own world over here.

90
00:07:48,340 --> 00:07:50,800
Sorry about the noise. That's okay.

91
00:07:52,020 --> 00:07:52,850
Okay.

92
00:07:52,933 --> 00:07:56,440
If Kirito were here, he'd get a big
kick out of this robot of yours.

93
00:07:56,540 --> 00:07:59,857
Actually, we built him because
the Commandante wanted us to.

94
00:07:59,940 --> 00:08:02,700
Wait, Kikuoka did? What for?

95
00:08:02,940 --> 00:08:07,317
It's a neat idea, actually, but I'm not
sure how serious he is about it yet.

96
00:08:07,400 --> 00:08:11,297
Ultimately, his goal is to bring Fluctlights
from the Underworld into our world.

97
00:08:11,380 --> 00:08:15,017
But the catch is, they're going to
need something they can move around in.

98
00:08:15,100 --> 00:08:19,137
So, wait, the plan is to
put the AIs in... That?

99
00:08:19,220 --> 00:08:20,300
Not this guy.

100
00:08:20,480 --> 00:08:22,597
He's just a prototype for data collection.

101
00:08:22,680 --> 00:08:26,445
We have a second robot with onboard
AI that's way more advanced.

102
00:08:26,580 --> 00:08:28,717
He operates a heck of a lot smoother.

103
00:08:28,800 --> 00:08:29,980
Oh, you don't say.

104
00:08:30,780 --> 00:08:33,640
I wonder what you
decided to call that one.

105
00:08:35,620 --> 00:08:37,840
Niemon, of course! Nie what?

106
00:08:38,140 --> 00:08:40,020
Oh, right. Nie means to.

107
00:08:40,460 --> 00:08:44,578
Anyway, why does having onboard AI
in this other robot make it better?

108
00:08:49,220 --> 00:08:52,517
For us to balance, our brains
make lots of micro-adjustments.

109
00:08:52,600 --> 00:08:54,837
To replicate that
mechanically would take a lot

110
00:08:54,920 --> 00:08:57,567
of tech and a bigger
body to house it all in.

111
00:08:59,020 --> 00:08:59,850
Oh.

112
00:09:00,180 --> 00:09:03,200
So if a Fluctlight is
piloting instead of a CPU,

113
00:09:03,580 --> 00:09:07,620
the robot can move more like a
human and also be smaller. Bingo!

114
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:12,237
And the smaller the tech inside, the
closer it can look like a human body.

115
00:09:12,320 --> 00:09:13,960
Or so we hope.

116
00:09:14,440 --> 00:09:16,734
For now, he's still a work in progress.

117
00:09:17,620 --> 00:09:19,337
Niemon's coming along, though.

118
00:09:19,420 --> 00:09:20,949
He's looking pretty human.

119
00:09:21,140 --> 00:09:23,117
Well, his silhouette does, anyway.

120
00:09:23,200 --> 00:09:25,837
And maybe one of these days
I'll get to see the damn thing.

121
00:09:25,920 --> 00:09:30,380
Wait, you haven't gotten it to walk
around on its own yet, have you? What?

122
00:09:30,580 --> 00:09:32,100
No, of course I haven't.

123
00:09:32,280 --> 00:09:34,840
His CPU's all loaded up and ready to go.

124
00:09:35,260 --> 00:09:38,457
But no one's home to work the
controls if you get my drift.

125
00:09:38,540 --> 00:09:39,370
Oh.

126
00:09:39,700 --> 00:09:40,840
Hey, Asuna. Huh?

127
00:09:41,280 --> 00:09:42,868
Have you had breakfast yet?

128
00:09:42,980 --> 00:09:44,200
No, I haven't.

129
00:09:44,380 --> 00:09:46,237
Then let's go down to
the cafeteria together.

130
00:09:46,320 --> 00:09:50,160
I'd invite Higa, but he already
made plans with Ichiemon.

131
00:09:52,280 --> 00:09:54,060
Bon appetit, ladies!

132
00:10:05,280 --> 00:10:06,640
Hm, back in a bit.

133
00:10:26,700 --> 00:10:28,060
Something wrong, Asuna?

134
00:10:28,840 --> 00:10:30,380
Oh, no, it's nothing.

135
00:10:30,920 --> 00:10:31,750
Come on!

136
00:10:53,440 --> 00:10:57,381
We've only been here for a day and
a half, but it feels way longer.

137
00:10:58,060 --> 00:11:00,380
Hey, how you doing over there?

138
00:11:00,960 --> 00:11:01,940
I don't know.

139
00:11:02,260 --> 00:11:04,613
This whole thing feels like a nightmare.

140
00:11:04,880 --> 00:11:09,040
I keep seeing Umber's arm flying
off and Ryo screaming as he died.

141
00:11:09,660 --> 00:11:11,542
Get that stuff out of your head.

142
00:11:11,900 --> 00:11:14,782
Start thinking about what
we're going to do next.

143
00:11:15,640 --> 00:11:17,522
I don't know what that could be.

144
00:11:19,960 --> 00:11:22,000
You know, you're absolutely right.

145
00:11:22,500 --> 00:11:25,117
We have to find a way to
break out of this cell,

146
00:11:25,200 --> 00:11:27,729
and then figure out
what happened to Alice.

147
00:11:28,300 --> 00:11:29,130
Yeah.

148
00:11:29,213 --> 00:11:31,581
If there's a way out of
this place, we'll find it.

149
00:11:32,680 --> 00:11:36,200
I wonder, did they bring
Alice here eight years ago?

150
00:11:36,780 --> 00:11:38,240
I don't know. Maybe.

151
00:11:39,980 --> 00:11:43,840
Since you brought her up, I just
want to be sure of something.

152
00:11:44,460 --> 00:11:47,440
The night that calls
herself Alice Synthesis 30,

153
00:11:48,360 --> 00:11:51,937
you're positive that she's the
same Alice you're looking for?

154
00:11:52,020 --> 00:11:53,140
Yeah, I am.

155
00:11:53,540 --> 00:11:58,180
Those blue eyes, golden hair, and
that voice, I'd never forget them.

156
00:11:58,400 --> 00:12:00,977
But she seemed like a
totally different person.

157
00:12:01,060 --> 00:12:05,577
For someone who's supposed to be your
childhood friend, she whacked you pretty good.

158
00:12:05,660 --> 00:12:07,097
But if you want my opinion,

159
00:12:07,180 --> 00:12:10,537
it could be she's under some kind
of mind control or something.

160
00:12:10,620 --> 00:12:14,177
But I don't remember seeing spells
like that in any of our textbooks.

161
00:12:14,260 --> 00:12:18,097
Right, but the high-ranking priests
in the church can manipulate life.

162
00:12:18,180 --> 00:12:21,592
If they can do that, they can
control someone's mind, too.

163
00:12:21,860 --> 00:12:26,540
Although, if that night really is
your Alice, whose voice did I hear?

164
00:12:27,340 --> 00:12:30,060
Two years ago, in the cave.

165
00:12:31,920 --> 00:12:34,640
Kirito, Yujiro, come and find me.

166
00:12:35,140 --> 00:12:40,520
I am waiting at the top
of the Central Cathedral.

167
00:12:44,280 --> 00:12:46,640
I will wait there for you both.

168
00:12:47,780 --> 00:12:48,610
Right.

169
00:12:48,693 --> 00:12:49,800
You told me that.

170
00:12:50,200 --> 00:12:52,260
When you and Selka were healing me,

171
00:12:52,380 --> 00:12:55,797
you said you heard a voice and then
saw something that looked like Alice.

172
00:12:55,880 --> 00:12:59,939
Yeah, she said she'd wait for us at
the top of the Central Cathedral.

173
00:13:00,160 --> 00:13:01,580
And now we're stuck.

174
00:13:08,900 --> 00:13:12,557
Hey, do you think we can access
the Stacia windows on these chains?

175
00:13:12,640 --> 00:13:14,640
I never even thought to try that.

176
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:16,440
Give it a shot. Okay.

177
00:13:21,200 --> 00:13:22,900
Whoa, it worked.

178
00:13:27,480 --> 00:13:31,068
We could pull on these chains
forever and they'd never budge.

179
00:13:31,160 --> 00:13:33,297
If we're going to break free of them,

180
00:13:33,380 --> 00:13:37,498
we need to get our hands on a tool
or weapon that's at least Class 38.

181
00:13:39,800 --> 00:13:41,506
Yeah, that won't do anything.

182
00:13:46,620 --> 00:13:48,157
I know what you're thinking,

183
00:13:48,240 --> 00:13:51,357
but the only things we have
in here are a couple of beds,

184
00:13:51,440 --> 00:13:53,197
water skins, and these chains.

185
00:13:53,280 --> 00:13:54,560
A pair of chains.

186
00:14:00,640 --> 00:14:02,120
Yeah, you're right.

187
00:14:02,300 --> 00:14:03,476
We got these chains.

188
00:14:03,600 --> 00:14:04,835
Two of these suckers.

189
00:14:04,940 --> 00:14:06,120
Just what we need.

190
00:14:06,820 --> 00:14:07,650
What?

191
00:14:18,160 --> 00:14:18,990
Hang on.

192
00:14:19,073 --> 00:14:20,077
I have a question.

193
00:14:20,160 --> 00:14:23,077
Is your idea to use the
chains against one another?

194
00:14:23,160 --> 00:14:24,400
It totally is.

195
00:14:24,640 --> 00:14:27,157
These chains of ours have
the same durability level.

196
00:14:27,240 --> 00:14:31,652
We'd need something with an object
control authority over 40 to break them.

197
00:14:31,860 --> 00:14:35,801
But if we snap them against each
other, that should wear them down.

198
00:14:36,160 --> 00:14:37,780
Just follow my lead, okay?

199
00:14:38,760 --> 00:14:39,590
Uh...

200
00:14:44,400 --> 00:14:45,520
Ready, and...

201
00:14:47,660 --> 00:14:48,540
Hell yeah!

202
00:14:48,760 --> 00:14:49,640
Not so loud.

203
00:14:49,980 --> 00:14:51,451
You'll wake the guard up.

204
00:14:59,660 --> 00:15:01,189
Let's give it another try.

205
00:15:04,960 --> 00:15:06,040
Ready and...

206
00:15:11,820 --> 00:15:15,291
I think that knocked at least
a hundred points off my life.

207
00:15:16,480 --> 00:15:19,777
That's a small price to pay
for freedom, wouldn't you say?

208
00:15:19,860 --> 00:15:21,154
Things are looking up.

209
00:15:24,800 --> 00:15:25,860
All right, then.

210
00:15:29,460 --> 00:15:32,320
If we do this, there's
no going back for us.

211
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:37,529
Remember, by breaking out of this cell
and looking for the truth about Alice,

212
00:15:38,300 --> 00:15:41,280
we're defying the Axiom
Church and its laws.

213
00:15:42,140 --> 00:15:46,493
That means from now on, there's no
time for second-guessing or hesitation.

214
00:15:47,280 --> 00:15:50,221
You better make sure you're
prepared for that now.

215
00:15:51,120 --> 00:15:53,002
Otherwise, you should stay here.

216
00:15:54,340 --> 00:15:56,000
Yeah, I know.

217
00:15:56,700 --> 00:15:58,200
But my mind's made up.

218
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:03,353
If I can return home with Alice, defying
the church isn't even a question.

219
00:16:04,060 --> 00:16:07,020
I'll even draw my sword
against them if I have to.

220
00:16:07,820 --> 00:16:10,173
I want to make sure that night is Alice.

221
00:16:10,360 --> 00:16:14,420
And if she is, I'll find a way to
change her back to the way she was.

222
00:16:14,860 --> 00:16:18,757
That's the only thing that matters
to me, and nothing will stop me.

223
00:16:18,840 --> 00:16:22,311
Remember what you said on that
picnic with Ronier and Tise?

224
00:16:22,880 --> 00:16:26,821
There are things you should do,
even if the laws say you shouldn't.

225
00:16:27,060 --> 00:16:29,420
I understand what you meant by that now.

226
00:16:30,940 --> 00:16:31,780
All right.

227
00:16:37,380 --> 00:16:39,027
You sound like you're ready.

228
00:16:39,480 --> 00:16:41,400
So let's go give them some hell.

229
00:16:55,360 --> 00:16:56,190
Sweet.

230
00:16:56,273 --> 00:16:57,797
Let's go before the guard wakes up.

231
00:16:57,880 --> 00:16:58,710
Right.

232
00:17:45,520 --> 00:17:47,917
It doesn't look like
anyone's following us.

233
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:51,000
No way, look at that. What's
up? Is someone coming?

234
00:17:52,180 --> 00:17:53,340
See these flowers?

235
00:17:55,060 --> 00:17:56,260
I've heard of them.

236
00:17:57,580 --> 00:18:00,580
Kirito, these are roses. Oh, yeah.

237
00:18:01,940 --> 00:18:02,880
No way!

238
00:18:03,100 --> 00:18:04,160
They are roses.

239
00:18:04,500 --> 00:18:06,680
And this place is chock full of them.

240
00:18:06,840 --> 00:18:09,605
It's rare to find one,
but a whole garden full?

241
00:18:10,560 --> 00:18:12,820
I can't believe we're standing here.

242
00:18:13,680 --> 00:18:17,380
You and I actually made it to
the Central Cathedral. Yeah.

243
00:18:17,840 --> 00:18:19,897
We're criminals, not Integrity Knights.

244
00:18:19,980 --> 00:18:22,097
But we're here, and
that's all that matters.

245
00:18:22,180 --> 00:18:25,357
It's probably for the best that
things worked out this way.

246
00:18:25,440 --> 00:18:29,237
If we had become Integrity Knights,
we might have ended up like Alice.

247
00:18:29,320 --> 00:18:33,077
They could have gotten in our heads
and screwed with our memories, too.

248
00:18:33,160 --> 00:18:36,460
I wonder, if they do that to
all the Integrity Knights,

249
00:18:36,680 --> 00:18:40,020
do they forget everything
about who they were before?

250
00:18:41,200 --> 00:18:42,140
Who knows?

251
00:18:42,700 --> 00:18:43,530
Yeah, well,

252
00:18:43,680 --> 00:18:46,177
even if a Knight's memories
got blocked somehow,

253
00:18:46,260 --> 00:18:50,557
they'd at least remember their parents,
or the place where they were born.

254
00:18:50,640 --> 00:18:53,300
Stuff like that's baked
into a person's soul.

255
00:18:53,620 --> 00:18:57,617
It'd be impossible to swap out those
kind of details with fake ones.

256
00:18:57,700 --> 00:18:58,940
You have a point.

257
00:18:59,260 --> 00:19:02,097
Those fake memories would
likely be tenuous at best.

258
00:19:02,180 --> 00:19:07,062
What if they were flying around while on
duty and came upon the place they grew up?

259
00:19:07,300 --> 00:19:11,476
Once they saw it, they would know,
and all their memories would come...

260
00:19:13,220 --> 00:19:14,050
What?

261
00:19:14,940 --> 00:19:15,820
Not again.

262
00:19:19,100 --> 00:19:20,160
I get it.

263
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:25,037
You're worried I'll find a way to get my
memories back in that tower, aren't you?

264
00:19:25,120 --> 00:19:25,950
No.

265
00:19:26,033 --> 00:19:27,200
Well, a little.

266
00:19:30,380 --> 00:19:34,160
Would you relax? Don't.
Stop it. Let me go.

267
00:19:34,720 --> 00:19:37,820
Man, I told you before not
to worry, and I meant it.

268
00:19:37,980 --> 00:19:40,215
Whether I get my memories back or not,

269
00:19:40,320 --> 00:19:43,967
we make a great team, so we're
sticking together till the end.

270
00:19:44,720 --> 00:19:46,297
Stop treating me like a kid?

271
00:19:46,380 --> 00:19:49,317
It's not that I don't trust
you to keep your word.

272
00:19:49,400 --> 00:19:52,277
You've only mentioned it
a million times so far.

273
00:19:52,360 --> 00:19:57,177
But when I think about how our
journey might be coming to an end?

274
00:19:57,260 --> 00:19:58,517
I feel...

275
00:19:58,600 --> 00:19:59,760
I don't know

276
00:20:00,620 --> 00:20:02,897
The fact is, it's gonna end.

277
00:20:02,980 --> 00:20:04,000
One day!

278
00:20:04,920 --> 00:20:07,273
But don't forget what that's gonna mean?

279
00:20:07,720 --> 00:20:09,677
You'll get Alice's memory back.

280
00:20:09,760 --> 00:20:11,878
And then you're gonna take her home.

281
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:16,217
There's another good thing
that'll come out of it.

282
00:20:16,300 --> 00:20:18,057
You'll get to pick another calling

283
00:20:18,140 --> 00:20:20,258
It might last the rest of your life.

284
00:20:20,420 --> 00:20:23,157
So you better start
thinking about what you want

285
00:20:23,240 --> 00:20:25,887
I think I still have a
bit of time to decide.

286
00:20:26,360 --> 00:20:30,242
I know whatever I pick won't have
anything to do with woodcutting.

287
00:20:30,420 --> 00:20:31,997
No surprise there.

288
00:20:32,080 --> 00:20:33,492
Come on, let's get going

289
00:20:45,620 --> 00:20:50,200
As expected, I have to admire
my Lady Alice's wisdom.

290
00:20:50,940 --> 00:20:53,777
Everyone thought escape from
that prison was impossible,

291
00:20:53,860 --> 00:20:56,860
and yet my mentor predicted it. Mentor?

292
00:20:57,620 --> 00:21:02,267
She ordered me to camp out here for the
night in anticipation of your breakout.

293
00:21:03,040 --> 00:21:08,080
To be honest, I was skeptical you'd
show up, and oh, how wrong I was.

294
00:21:14,200 --> 00:21:15,640
An Integrity Knight?

295
00:21:16,100 --> 00:21:18,240
His mentor is Alice?

296
00:21:18,640 --> 00:21:22,320
That said, you'll be returning
to your gloomy prison shortly.

297
00:21:22,600 --> 00:21:26,060
After I administer punishment
for your transgressions.

298
00:21:28,200 --> 00:21:30,671
You've been warned, so prepare yourselves.

299
00:21:31,040 --> 00:21:33,037
Well, here's a warning for you, then.

300
00:21:33,120 --> 00:21:37,355
If you think we're going to go back
there without a fight, you're crazy.

301
00:21:42,460 --> 00:21:43,540
Such nerve!

302
00:21:43,880 --> 00:21:46,880
In honor of your bravado,
I shall introduce myself.

303
00:21:50,720 --> 00:21:54,500
I am the Integrity Knight
Eldrie Synthesis 31.

304
00:21:54,960 --> 00:21:57,680
I do not have a territory to my name yet,

305
00:21:57,920 --> 00:22:00,449
as I was freshly summoned
only a month ago.

306
00:22:01,980 --> 00:22:04,440
I do hope that fact doesn't bother you.

307
00:22:23,400 --> 00:22:26,800
Let's do it.

308
00:23:26,700 --> 00:23:29,120
The Alice to you
